summary:
  A play or a step opens its list right up to the newest segment.

history:
  Measured on Qt 6.12 with FFmpeg 9: the list's reader runs 4.0 to 4.5 s
  ahead of the sound, and a player stopped on a list whose reader has run out
  of segments holds the whole widget until the list grows. An open has to land
  twelve seconds short of the newest segment, which leaves the next beats time
  to grow the list before the reader is at its end.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SlideLogic.js

find:
      var oldest = first * SEG_MS + KEEP_MS, newest = (last + 1) * SEG_MS - OPEN_GAP_MS;

replace:
      var oldest = first * SEG_MS + KEEP_MS, newest = (last + 1) * SEG_MS;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_slidelogic.qml::test_an_open_keeps_clear_of_both_ends.
